- Kernel body, math, and `asc2.full` constant tile are **unchanged** — so the 353024 B measurement still applies directly.
- Correctness is provable, not probabilistic: the factored form produces bit-identical per-element results to the 100%-passing original (same `w=exp(-|x|)`, same per-branch `num`/`den`, same `y`); it only blends `num` and `den` separately then divides once, instead of blending two pre-computed quotients. For the selected branch the `/` operands are identical → identical result.
- `where`/compare destinations at T=1280 are 5120 B (5120 % 256 == 0) → the destination-overrun defect is clear; all 20 cases have ≥1M elements (≥782 tiles ≫ 72 cores) so 72-core saturation is preserved.

